Subject: [PATCH] Release the factory reference of chain normalizer links

mlt_chain_attach_normalizers() creates each normalizer link with
mlt_factory_link(), which returns a link with one reference, and then
attaches it with mlt_chain_attach(), which takes its own reference
(mlt_properties_inc_ref). The factory's reference is never released, so
when the chain closes the links' reference count drops from 2 to 1 and
the links (with their properties, scalers and resamplers) are never
freed.

Every other caller of mlt_chain_attach() releases its own reference
afterwards (the XML producer's <link> handling, producer_melt and
Mlt::Chain::attach). Do the same here.

Measured on Windows by opening and closing a chain with the normalizer
links repeatedly: each closed chain kept about 377 process handles (each
property owns a mutex) before this change and none after it. Rendered
frames are unchanged.
---
diff --git a/src/framework/mlt_chain.c b/src/framework/mlt_chain.c
index fafb93db..aa3137a3 100644
--- a/src/framework/mlt_chain.c
+++ b/src/framework/mlt_chain.c
@@ -476,6 +476,9 @@ extern void mlt_chain_attach_normalizers(mlt_chain self)
                 mlt_properties_set_int(MLT_LINK_PROPERTIES(link), "_loader", 1);
                 mlt_chain_attach(self, link);
                 mlt_chain_move_link(self, mlt_chain_link_count(self) - 1, norm_count);
+                // The chain holds its own reference now (mlt_chain_attach): release the factory's, as every other
+                // caller of mlt_chain_attach does, or the link outlives the chain.
+                mlt_link_close(link);
                 norm_count++;
                 break;
             }
